  <h1>Gated DeltaNet-2: Untying Erase and Write in Linear Attention</h1>
  <p class="lead">Linear attention compresses history into a fixed-size state matrix — a key-value memory that must accommodate thousands of associations in constant space. Every prior delta-rule model (DeltaNet, Gated DeltaNet, KDA) uses a single scalar gate to control both erasing stale content and writing new content. Gated DeltaNet-2 (NVIDIA, 2026) separates these into a channel-wise erase gate b_t and write gate w_t, achieving sharper long-context retrieval while preserving efficient chunkwise training.</p>
